{% extends "_layouts/layout.njk" %}
{% set pageTitle = "Old Timey Mono" %}

{% block main %}
    <div class="container" style="max-width: 65ch;">
        <h2>
            Get It
        </h2>
        <p>
            <a class="btn btn-success" href="https://github.com/dse/old-timey-mono-font/releases" target="_blank">Download</a>
            <a class="btn btn-primary" href="https://github.com/dse/old-timey-mono-font" target="_blank">GitHub</a>
        </p>
        <h2>
            Old Timey Mono
        </h2>
        <p>
            Old Timey Mono is a faithful monoline revival of Reproducing Typewriter (1906),
            a typeface for simulating typewritten copy in advertising brochures, junk mail, etc.
            It's also the typeface used in the Turbo Pascal 3.0 manual.
        </p>
        <h2>
            Old Timey Code
        </h2>
        <p>
            Old Timey Code is based on Old Timey Mono, and was intended
            for coding, developing, programming, whatever you call it.
        </p>
        <p>
            Reproducing Typewriter was developed for simulating typewritten copy
            in advertising brochures and whatnot, in letters sent to a bulk
            mailing list, and for other purposes.  Shorter serifs and (in some
            cases) more open arpetures help the typeface survive the
            imperfections resulting from reproduction, especially at smaller
            point sizes.
        </p>
        <p>
            I think those features make it a pretty good typeface for coding,
            though I had to make additional changes.
        </p>
        <h2>
            You Know You Want It
        </h2>
        <p>
            <a class="btn btn-success" href="https://github.com/dse/old-timey-mono-font/releases" target="_blank">Download</a>
            <a class="btn btn-primary" href="https://github.com/dse/old-timey-mono-font" target="_blank">GitHub</a>
        </p>
    </div>
    <div class="container" style="max-width: 65ch;">
        <h2>
            Character Coverage
        </h2>
        <ul>
            <li>
                Covers almost all Western European languages using Greek,
                Cyrillic, and Latin scripts.
                <ul>
                    <li>
                        Full support for WGL4, AGLFN, MES-1.  (Except ligatures.)
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        Near complete support for W1G, SECS, MES-2.
                    </li>
                </ul>
            </li>
            <li>
                Unicode box drawing, block drawing, braille, IPA, and everything
                in Code Page 437 (MS-DOS).
            </li>
            <li>
                Additional math symbols and geometric shapes.
            </li>
            <li>
                A few cool surprises.
            </li>
        </ul>
    </div>
{% endblock %}
